{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise-hyperplane","title":"prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise-hyperplane","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3327,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise-hyperplane","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise-hyperplane","line":5786,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Signature of a Hypersurface's Tangent Space]\n\\label{prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise-hyperplane}\n\n\\uses{prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise, lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line}\n\n\n\n\nLet $(V,q)$ have signature $(r,s)$, let $W$ be a hyperplane, and let $0\\ne x\\in W^\\perp$. If $(r',s')$ is the signature of $q|_W$, then a positive $x$ gives $r'+1=r$, $s'=s$, while a negative $x$ gives $r'=r$, $s'+1=s$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise,lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line}\n\\sketch Lemma \\ref{lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line} identifies $W$ with $\\operatorname{span}(x)^\\perp$; apply Proposition \\ref{prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Signature of a Hypersurface&#x27;s Tangent Space] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a6879706572737572666163652d7369676e61747572652d706f696e74776973652d6879706572706c616e65\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahypersurface-signature-pointwise\">↗ prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line\">↗ lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(V,q)$\">$(V,q)$</span> have signature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r,s)$\">$(r,s)$</span>, let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> be a hyperplane, and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\ne x\\in W^\\perp $\">$0\\ne x\\in W^\\perp $</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r&#x27;,s&#x27;)$\">$(r&#x27;,s&#x27;)$</span> is the signature of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q|_W$\">$q|_W$</span>, then a positive <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r&#x27;+1=r$\">$r&#x27;+1=r$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s&#x27;=s$\">$s&#x27;=s$</span>, while a negative <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r&#x27;=r$\">$r&#x27;=r$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s&#x27;+1=s$\">$s&#x27;+1=s$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahypersurface-signature-pointwise\">↗ prop:hypersurface-signature-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line\">↗ lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line</a> \\sket